      "writtenOn": "2021-06-17T12:13:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s very hacky.. Each host apex is passed to microdroid as a partition in a payload disk image. Apexd needs to know the original file\u0027s size to open it as a zip archive, but when it is passed as a block device, the size is aligned to 4k boundary (losing the original size info). At first, I encoded the size info of payload apexes in metadata partition, but making apexd to open block-device apexes by reading size from somewhere else was not easy. (Too many changes required)  That\u0027s why we put the size at the end of each block device.",
      "parentUuid": "c09928e7_cd1d01d5",
